[0.000, "o", "ization attempt, plus a deploy log. First a coarse picture: which\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mnon-approved codes appear on which node. A throwaway Python snippet is enough for that.\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[36m▸\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1mbash\u001b[22m\u001b[39m python3 - <<'EOF'\u001b[2m … (+10 lines)\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m\u001b[2m… 9 more lines\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-3  51_insufficient_funds  645\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-3  54_expired_card        621\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-3  E_TLS_HANDSHAKE        7814\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-3  E_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT     129\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-4  05_do_not_honor        674\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-4  51_insufficient_funds  647\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-4  54_expired_card        678\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90mgw-4  E_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT     121\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[3mThe declines and upstream timeouts look the same on every node, so t"]
[0.000, "o", "hey are background noise. The only outlier is\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mE_TLS_HANDSHAKE, 7,814 of them, all on gw-3. A TLS failure that appears on exactly one node smells like a\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mconfiguration or certificate change. Let me look at the deploy log for the night.\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[36m▸\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1mbash\u001b[22m\u001b[39m grep -E 'T0[1-4]:' logs/deploy.log\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m\u001b[2m… 1 more lines\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T02:09:41Z gw-3 cert-manager: renewing client certificate for acquirer=nordbank (expires 2026-10-19)\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T02:09:58Z gw-3 cert-manager: installed client certificate for acquirer=nordbank serial=4F:A1:07:3C:9\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T02:10:00Z gw-3 tls-pool: reloaded 3 upstream pools\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T02:40:17Z gw-4 config-sync: ok (rev 4472)\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T03:38:55Z gw-3 operator(oncall-mira): "]
[0.001, "o", "cert-manager pin acquirer=nordbank serial=2B:77:E0:11:04\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T03:41:12Z gw-3 cert-manager: installed client certificate for acquirer=nordbank serial=2B:77:E0:11:0\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T03:41:13Z gw-3 tls-pool: reloaded 3 upstream pools\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m\u001b[90m2026-10-12T04:18:30Z gw-1 gc: long pause 1.2s (heap 3.1G)\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[3mThere it is: at 02:09:58 gw-3 installed a renewed nordbank client certificate issued by 'Payments Issuing CA G2', and\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mat 03:41:12 on-call pinned back a G1 certificate. nordbank apparently does not trust G2. I want the exact window,\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mconfirmation that only gw-3 to nordbank is affected, and the impact per merchant. I'll write a small script so the\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[2;3mnumbers can be reproduced and rerun.\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n  \u001b[36m▸\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1mwrite\u001b[22m\u001b[39m analyze.py \u001b[2m(49 lines)\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2m    │ \u001b[22m"]
